  "result": "I implemented `satisfies(version, range)` in `src/semver.js` following `docs/SPEC.md`, and `npm test` passes (110 passed, 0 failed).\n\nI added `test/satisfies.test.js` with 109 cases. They cover:\n- version parsing and invalid input\n- prerelease ordering\n- `||` sets and whitespace\n- x-ranges and partial versions with operators\n- tilde, caret and hyphen ranges\n- the prerelease same-tuple rule\n\nThe spec doesn't say what to do in a few cases, so I made these calls:\n- **Prerelease identifiers:** numeric identifiers with leading zeros, like `1.0.0-01`, are accepted, because the spec only lists the allowed characters.\n- **Wildcards in the middle:** a wildcard makes every later position a wildcard, so `1.x.3` is treated as `1.x`.\n- **Partial version with a prerelease:** `1.2-beta` is invalid.\n- **Operator spacing:** a space between the operator and the version (`>= 1.2.3`) is allowed only for `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=` and `=`. `~ 1.2.3` and `^ 1.2.3` are invalid.\n- **Unsatisfiable operators:** `>*` and `<*` match nothing.\n- **Empty alternatives:** an empty alternative, as in `1.0.0 ||`, matches any non-prerelease version.",
